# Aderyn triage — acknowledged finding instances, one key per line.
#
# Covers every high-severity finding, plus the low-severity detectors promoted
# to gating in wall/script/gate_aderyn.py.
#
# Key format: detector_name|contract_path|line_no|anchor
#
# The anchor is a digest of the source line the finding sits on, with
# whitespace collapsed. It records the text the finding was accepted against,
# so a key that only moved can be told apart from a key whose code changed.
#
# This file records review decisions: a finding is read, judged a false positive
# or an accepted risk, and the key committed here with the reasoning above it.
#
# Stability: aderyn anchors an instance at the offending statement, so any
# insertion or deletion above it — inside the function body or above the
# function itself — shifts the line number. `make retriage` re-anchors those,
# pairing on the digest and never on the number. A key whose digest no longer
# appears is a finding whose code changed, and is re-reviewed rather than
# silently inherited.
#
# Empty: the aderyn lane is staged off in wall/wall.mk while its backlog is
# reviewed. Nothing has been accepted yet.
